Subject: [PATCH] editor: integrate ZLS through the authenticated daemon connection

Add native completion, diagnostics, hover, definitions and references for Zig
and ZON buffers. Run ZLS on the project host; bind process ownership to the
connection and reclaim idle sessions. Synchronize unsaved buffers with UTF-16
positions and document versions, and reject stale query results.

Keep Zig/ZLS optional. Detect incompatible toolchains and expose restart/error
status in the editor. Respect ZLS configuration and project check steps for
compiler diagnostics. Gate clients on a nativeZls daemon capability.

Includes protocol, stdio framing/lifecycle, real ZLS, daemon end-to-end, and
CodeMirror browser regression tests. Apply after the native Zig grammar patch.

